ENG-16  Mouse look: while a game hides the cursor, the real pointer is detached from the mouse and stays where the game put it, so it never reaches the Dock, the menu bar or a hot corner.
Component: lby-octavia-gcmouse (input), patches/engine/lby-octavia-gcmouse/.

dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h, cocoa_app.m, mouse.c (winemac.so). Adapted 2026-11-15 from kit/patches/wine-winemac-mouselook.patch of
github.com/sirdankdabs/bo-mac (MIT; its notice stays with the idea), ported by hand to Dormison r7 plus our series. LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

What: in native full screen a game in mouse look (the cursor hidden and clipped) saw the pointer follow the mouse to the screen's edge and the Dock
or the menu bar come out, the game losing focus. Dormison hides the Dock and the menu bar for such a game, but not in native full screen (it returns
early there, updatePresentationOptionsForActive), and macOS 27 ignores the Dock option in native full screen (S14). This patch removes the cause: after the
first CGWarpMouseCursorPosition the mouse is detached from the cursor (CGAssociateMouseAndMouseCursorPosition(false), mouseLook) and every move goes
to the game as a delta; the game's own SetCursorPos calls to the point it put the cursor at (its recentring, 160 times a second) do nothing while the look lasts, which also spares the
WindowServer a warp each time (1000 Hz mouse aiming felt heavy); a SetCursorPos anywhere else (a menu drawing its own pointer, RE9) moves the cursor as before, the look
ends and starts again there (first version ignored every call and the pointer in RE9's menu teleported, owner's test 2026-11-15). Clicks and scroll carry no position (INT_MIN) while it lasts. The look ends, and
the mouse is attached again (and the cursor, hidden with CGDisplayHideCursor for the look, shown again), when the cursor is shown, the app deactivates, a window is dragged or the game moves the cursor itself without hiding it.
Requires: nothing. Interplay with ENG-08 (GCMouse, 0004: both change how moves reach the game) not checked yet.
Other bases: Dormison's cocoa_app.m (the clip handler WineCursorRestrictionClipCursorHandler does not warp; the event-tap handler has its own setCursorPosition and is not changed).
Test: RE9 (D3DMetal) in native full screen, mouse look with the cursor hidden: push the mouse to every edge and corner for a minute, the Dock and the menu bar
must not come out and the game must keep focus; open a menu (cursor shown) and come back; PEAK, Isaac and ETS 2 unchanged; the pointer shown again after Cmd-Tab.
Log: one line `lullaby:mouselook begin|end|setpos-ends anchor x,y other x,y flag N` in the wine log at each start and end of the look (rare, at most 400 a run).
Verified on: RE9 (2026-11-15): Dock and menu bar stay hidden when the mouse is pushed to the bottom edge; RE9's menu pointer jumped to the centre whenever the mouse stood still: win32u's GetCursorPos asks the driver after 100 ms without a move and got the detached pointer's place; GetCursorPos now keeps Wine's own position during the look (macdrv_get_cursor_position returns 2).
Owner 2026-11-15 (v5): now and then a motionless system arrow stood at the anchor, in a scene and in a menu (Wine counted the cursor hidden, macOS drew it); CGDisplayHideCursor/ShowCursor now pair with the look.
Switch: LULLABY_MOUSELOOK=0 as a launch option turns it off for a run; on by default (a fix of a plain fault).

